It's more use than you think. There are a number of items that
can be usefully cursed:

  1) Cursed scrolls of teleport will level teleport - very useful
     for "getting down"

    ** BUT ** I don't waste unholy water cursing teleport scrolls
    because the same effect can be generated if you read the scroll
    while confused, leading to point #2....

  2) A cursed unicorn horn is very useful - BUT MAKE SURE YOU ALSO
     HAVE AN UNCURSED ONE!!  Repeated applications of the cursed
     horn (followed by the other one to cure unwanted effects) will
     eventually get you confused.  Just the ticket for level teleporting,
     or rustproofing Mjollnir, your armor, etc.

  3) Cursed scrolls of genocide allow you to create lots of monsters.
     Often used to produce a roomful of juicy wraiths or helpful nurses.

  4) A cursed potion of gain level will send you upstairs.  Among other
     things, this is handy when you have paralyzed the Wizard and he
     happens to be standing on the stairs.   Unfortunately, it won't
     work on level one when you have the amulet (a bug IMHO), forcing
     you to drop a few more jewels before you head up to the endgame.

